{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.char_seven_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.char_seven_forces","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.lean#L155-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.numerators_original_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.numerators_original_form","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.lean#L112-L138","doc":"Route 11 end to end: from the original `2·L wₖ + L (−wₖ)` to `mₖ·L1`,\nwith the `7` cleared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.sum_of_numerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.sum_of_numerators","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.lean#L79-L95","doc":"Summing the three numerators: `17 + 5 − 1 = 21`, and `21/7 = 3`.\n\nIn the `π²` normalisation this is `Σₖ Re[2L(wₖ)+L(−wₖ)] = π²/2 = 3·L(1)`, which is\nRoute 8's target and hence the 5₂ sum rule. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fivetwo-level-seven-ladder","label":"prop:fivetwo-level-seven-ladder","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/fivetwo-level-seven-ladder.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.numerators_of_five_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.numerators_of_five_term","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenLadder.lean#L49-L77","doc":"The three level-7 numerators, from three five-term instances plus reflection.\n\n`L1` stands for `L 1`; it is kept abstract so the statement needs no evaluation.\n\nThe targets are stated **with the `7` cleared**, as `7·Tₖ = mₖ·L1`. Dividing by\n`7` would need `Field R` *and* `CharZero R` — in characteristic `7` the divided\nform is false, and `ring` correctly refuses it. Cleared, the certificate has\n**integer** coefficients and the result holds over any `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}